# Portfolio docs — update every prompt

In this workspace, treat these two files as mandatory session memory:

1. `ReadmeProject.md` — developer guide: what each file / function / code block is for
2. `ProjectMemory.md` — Cursor / AI chronological memory of every change (handoff across chats)

## Required docs behavior

- At the start of work that touches this project, read `ProjectMemory.md` (and `ReadmeProject.md` when structure matters).
- On **every prompt** that results in any project change (code, config, content, docs, or decisions), update both files before finishing:
  - `ReadmeProject.md` — refresh purpose notes for any added/changed/removed files, functions, or code blocks so a developer can understand the project
  - `ProjectMemory.md` — add a dated entry at the top of the change log (what / why / files) so later sessions (even in another directory/chat) know history
- If the prompt only asks a question and no files change, still add a short note in `ProjectMemory.md` only when a useful decision or clarification was made; otherwise skip.
- Keep wording simple so the user can explain the project to others.
- Do not skip these updates even for small changes.

